1. fixed window counter - only n request are allowed in t sec and it resets to 0
   - cannot support burst load
2. Sliding window Log - when a request is made then time is attched and its queued, total number of request in 10 sec of silding exceeds or not. basically impl queuing
    - keep track of time and then queuing . so increase in memory leading to slowness
3. Sliding window counter - need not have queue or  timestamp. on moedal we should accept or not
divide the windows into parts and check the previous contribution and how many more we can accomodate
4. Token bucket - bucket is filled with token - total num supported, refill/sec  
5. leaky bucket - place it in the queue and then consumer will consume and their will be drain/sec
 -- latency
 -- uniform rate of consumption 


